{{/*
  Bootstrap gate.

  1Password-backed files are skipped until `op` can actually authenticate, so a
  fresh machine's first apply never fails on a secret it cannot reach yet. That
  first run installs packages (including the 1Password app) and lands every
  non-secret config; sign in, re-run `chezmoi apply`, and these files appear.

  This is evaluated on every apply rather than stored in chezmoi's config data,
  which is read once at init — so picking up the secrets needs no re-init.

  The check lives in `scripts/op-ready.sh` because it needs a bound and a
  progress notice, and neither fits in a one-liner. Asking `op whoami` inline
  with no bound hung every chezmoi command, silently, on a machine where the
  1Password desktop app was prompting for an approval nobody was looking at.
  `--debug` stopped after reading this file and said nothing further. A
  `|| echo notready` guard answers a non-zero exit, which is a different
  failure from never exiting.

  `output` fails the whole template on a non-zero exit, so the script always
  exits 0 and puts its verdict on stdout. `lookPath` returns an empty string
  rather than erroring when absent.
*/}}
{{- $opReady := false -}}
{{- if lookPath "op" -}}
{{-   $opReady = eq (output "sh" (joinPath .chezmoi.sourceDir "scripts/op-ready.sh") | trim) "ready" -}}
{{- end -}}
{{ if not $opReady }}
.ssh/server_ed25519
.ssh/github_ed25519
.ssh/authorized_keys
.claude/writing-voice.md
.aws/config
.config/llama/api-key
.local/share/atuin/key
{{- /* launchd loads every plist in LaunchAgents at login, so the plist waits
       here with the API key; otherwise a login before the key exists starts
       a server that fails every 30s. */}}
Library/LaunchAgents/local.llama-agent.plist
{{ end }}
